# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the debug build of the test client.
#
# GTK, GLib, and their dependencies allocate caches, type registrations,
# and theme data once at startup and never free them. That is by design
# in a library that expects the process to end, but the debug build
# links the address sanitizer, so every windowed run would otherwise
# finish with a page of leak reports and exit non-zero.
#
# Suppressed by library name rather than by turning leak detection off,
# so a leak in Disciple's own code is still reported. Used by
# `make run` and by the VS Code launch configuration.
#
# MIT License (see: LICENSE)
# Copyright (C) 2026 Tomaz Stih
#
leak:libgtk-3
leak:libgdk-3
leak:libgdk_pixbuf
leak:libglib-2.0
leak:libgobject-2.0
leak:libgio-2.0
leak:libfontconfig
leak:libpango
